---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Drone Exam: FAA Part 107 Prep Privacy Policy - Logicpath Systems">
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Drone Exam: FAA Part 107 Prep</strong></p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Last Updated:</strong> November 2026</p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <h2>Introduction</h2>
                    <p>Drone Exam: FAA Part 107 Prep (&ldquo;the App&rdquo;) is developed and maintained by LogicPath Systems. The App is supported by advertising. This policy explains what data the App and the Google services in it collect, how it is used, and the choices you have.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>1. Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
                    <p>You do not need an account to use the App. We do not ask for your name, email address, or phone number.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Study Data:</strong> Your quiz scores, streaks, points, saved mistakes, session history, and settings are stored on your device. We do not run a server that receives this data.</li>
                        <li><strong>Android Backup:</strong> If Android backup is turned on for your Google account, Android may include this data in your device backup and restore it to a new or reset device. Google manages that backup under your account, and we cannot access it.</li>
                        <li><strong>Tools:</strong> The coordinates you enter in the sunrise and twilight tool are used only for calculations on your device.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>2. Information Collected Automatically</h2>
                    <p>The Google services built into the App collect the following when you use it, subject to your choices in Section 4. This data is not anonymous: it does not include your name or email, but it can be linked to your device through identifiers.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Identifiers:</strong> Your device's advertising ID, app instance ID, and similar identifiers.</li>
                        <li><strong>Network and Location:</strong> Your IP address and an approximate location, such as your country or region, worked out from it.</li>
                        <li><strong>Device and App Information:</strong> Device model, operating system, language, app version, and how the App was installed.</li>
                        <li><strong>Usage:</strong> Which screens you open, app opens, session activity, and how you interact with ads.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
                    <p>The App is free and supported by ads served through Google AdMob. You may see:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Native ads on the dashboard, labeled &ldquo;Sponsored&rdquo;.</li>
                        <li>Full-screen ads when you finish a quiz or practice exam.</li>
                        <li>App-open ads when you return to the App.</li>
                        <li>Rewarded video ads, only if you choose to watch one for bonus points or extra flashcards.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Google and its partners may use the information in Section 2 to show, personalize, limit, and measure ads, and to prevent fraud. On supported Android versions, this may include Android's ad-related features for topics and attribution.</p>
                    <p>We ask Google not to show ads rated for mature audiences. We do not choose individual ads, and tapping an ad may take you to a third-party site or app with its own privacy practices.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>4. Your Ad Privacy Choices</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Consent:</strong> Where the law requires it, including in the European Economic Area, the UK, and Switzerland, the App shows a consent form from Google before requesting ads or starting analytics. If you decline personalized ads, you may still see non-personalized or limited ads.</li>
                        <li><strong>Change Your Choice:</strong> Where this option is required, go to Settings &gt; Ad Privacy Settings in the App at any time.</li>
                        <li><strong>Android Settings:</strong> You can reset or delete your advertising ID in your device's Google or privacy settings. The exact menu varies by device.</li>
                        <li><strong>Google Ad Settings:</strong> You can manage ad personalization for your Google account at <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">myadcenter.google.com</a>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Firebase Analytics stays off until your consent choice is known. Where consent is required, it runs only if you agree to all the purposes in the form, and it stops if you decline or later change your choice. Where consent is not required, it runs by default, and uninstalling the App stops it.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>5. How We Use Information</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>To provide the App's study features and tools.</li>
                        <li>To fund the free App through advertising.</li>
                        <li>To understand which screens and features are used, so we can improve them.</li>
                        <li>To remember your consent and app settings.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>
                    <p>These services receive data directly from the App and handle it under their own policies:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Google AdMob and User Messaging Platform:</strong> Advertising and consent. See the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">how Google uses data from apps that use its services</a>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Google Firebase Analytics:</strong> App usage analytics. See <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">Privacy and Security in Firebase</a>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Google Fonts:</strong> The App downloads its font from Google, which receives your IP address. See the <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">Google Fonts privacy FAQ</a>.</li>
                        <li><strong>AviationWeather.gov:</strong> A U.S. government weather service. When you look up METAR or TAF data, it receives the station code you enter and your IP address.</li>
                        <li><strong>Other Links:</strong> Links to the FAA, Google Play, and other websites open outside the App. When you use Share App, your device's share menu handles it.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>7. Sale and Sharing of Data</h2>
                    <p>We do not sell your data for money, and we do not receive your study data. Under some U.S. state laws, however, disclosing identifiers to advertising partners for personalized ads can count as a &ldquo;sale&rdquo; or &ldquo;sharing&rdquo; of personal information. You can limit this using the choices in Section 4.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>8. Permissions</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>The App uses internet and network status access, plus the advertising ID and Android ad services permissions added by Google's software.</li>
                        <li>Google's software also uses background permissions to send analytics and ad data reliably.</li>
                        <li>The App does not request access to your GPS location, camera, microphone, contacts, photos, or files.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>9. Data Retention, Deletion &amp; Security</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>To erase your study data, use Settings &gt; Reset All Progress Data or uninstall the App. A copy in your Android backup is removed separately through your Google account settings.</li>
                        <li>Google keeps the data it collects according to its own policies and the settings of its services.</li>
                        <li>Because the App has no accounts, we usually cannot match Google's data to you. You can still contact us with a request, and you can use the options in Section 4.</li>
                        <li>Weather requests use encrypted HTTPS connections. Study data is kept in the App's private device storage and is not separately encrypted. No method of storage or transmission is completely secure.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>10. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
                    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or limit the use of your personal data, to object to its use, and to complain to your data protection authority.</p>
                    <p>Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies, we rely on your consent for the advertising and analytics that require it. You can withdraw consent as described in Section 4.</p>
                    <p>Google may process data in the United States and other countries outside your own.</p>
                    <p>To make a request, email us at the address below.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2>
                    <p>This App is intended for users aged 16 and above, in line with the FAA's minimum age for a remote pilot certificate. It is not directed to children, and we tell Google not to treat its ads as child-directed. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information, contact us and we will help remove it.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>12. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
                    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will appear in the App with a new &ldquo;Last Updated&rdquo; date. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>13. Sources of Information</h2>
                    <p>All aviation-related content in this app is sourced from publicly available official FAA publications, including but not limited to:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>14 CFR Part 107 &mdash; Small Unmanned Aircraft Systems Rules (<a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-14/chapter-I/subchapter-F/part-107" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">ecfr.gov</a>)</li>
                        <li>FAA Remote Pilot Study Guide (FAA-G-8082-22) (<a href="https://www.faa.gov/uas/commercial_operators/become_a_drone_pilot" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">faa.gov</a>)</li>
                        <li>Advisory Circular AC 107-2A (<a href="https://www.faa.gov/documentLibrary/media/Advisory_Circular/AC_107-2A.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">faa.gov</a>)</li>
                        <li>FAA Aeronautical Chart Users' Guide (<a href="https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/flight_info/aeronav/digital_products/aero_guide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">faa.gov</a>)</li>
                        <li>FAA DroneZone &mdash; Registration &amp; Airspace Authorization (<a href="https://faadronezone.faa.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">faadronezone.faa.gov</a>)</li>
                        <li>Aviation Weather Center &mdash; METAR/TAF Data (<a href="https://aviationweather.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">aviationweather.gov</a>)</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>14. Important Disclaimer</h2>
                    <p>This app is an independent educational study tool developed and maintained by LogicPath Systems. It is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA), the U.S. Department of Transportation, or any other government agency. All information is sourced from publicly available FAA publications listed above and is provided for educational and exam preparation purposes only. Always refer to official FAA sources for the most current regulations.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
                    <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:</p>
                    <p>📧 <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);"><strong>contact@logicpathsystems.com</strong></a></p>
                    <p><strong>LogicPath Systems</strong></p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

